{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/805732-the-cast-of-peanuts-as-childling-changelings","id":805732,"title":"The Cast of \"Peanuts\" as Childling Changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-10T20:14:34-08:00","id":805732,"title":"The Cast of \"Peanuts\" as Childling Changelings","content":"Just saw &quot;The Peanuts Movie&quot; and thought to myself<br /> What Kith would &quot;the gang&quot; fit into as Childling Changelings?<br /> <br /> Here we go:<br /> Charlie Brown: Seelie Boogan (Kind honest hard working Everyman who never EVER gives up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> Snoopy: Seelie Beagle Pooka (A mischievous trickster and a good friend)<br /> Woodstock: Seelie Canary Pooka (Playful loyal avian friend)<br /> Sally Brown: Seelie Knocker (Lovable bossy little complainer and incurable romantic)<br /> Linus: Seelie Troll (Loyal, caring, patient, wise, honorable)<br /> Peppermint Patty: Seelie Satyr (Hyper energetic tomboy, stupid but well meaning)<br /> Marcie: Seelie Eshu (A font of warm calm esoteric wisdom)<br /> Schroeder: Seelie Sidhe (Dignified artistic chick magnet and poetic soul)<br /> Pigpen: Seelie Slaugh (Dirty messy but kind and misunderstood eccentric)<br /> Lucy: Unseelie Redcap (Hateful cynical sarcastic little bitch who gets off on bullying nice people)<br /> <br /> Say, that's quite an idea to kickstart (hehehe) a chronicle!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 01-10-2016, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T23:02:19-08:00","id":805829,"title":"","content":"careful or people will ask about Simpsons, Detective conan, etc... <br /> <br /> Bart is definitely an unseelie... I dont know what kith... Conan is certainly seelie, possibly a sidhe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T01:14:10-08:00","id":805890,"title":"","content":"Redcap may be the obvious answer due to Bart's weary cynicism towards life, but frankly his enthusiasm energy and devil-may-care attitude gravitates more towards the Satyr.... though I DO agree on the Unseelie Part.<br /> <br /> Edogawa Conan.... His inquisitive, intelligent, and above all logical (not to mention technologically adept and scientific) approach towards solving crimes actually implies more Knocker than anything else, and that also includes his deadpan, condescending attitude. That said, the same can be said about particularly arrogant Sidhe of both alignments.<br /> <br /> Getting back on track:<br /> The Little Redhead Girl? Oh yes she is DEFINITELY a Seelie Sidhe, to so easily steal Charlie Brown's Heart. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T02:35:10-08:00","id":805923,"title":"","content":"True theirs a whole article on TVtropes.com <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Flanderization\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...Flanderization</a><br /> <br /> Oh yes<br /> The little redhead girl does she ever make an appearance? ever? at this point, or she still just &quot;Mentioned, but not seen&quot; Kind of like we only hear &quot;Blah blah blah&quot; Come out of the grown ups mouths...<br /> <br /> Not seen the new movie though I Probaly should not seen chalie brown at all since I was little...<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh is the trick snoop does with his ears, a possible interprutation of the wayfare Art, or maybe a 5 dot specialty &quot;Wings Merit&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T04:58:50-08:00","id":805987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/805732-the-cast-of-peanuts-as-childling-changelings?p=805923#post805923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True theirs a whole article on TVtropes.com <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Flanderization\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...Flanderization</a><br /> <br /> Oh yes<br /> The little redhead girl does she ever make an appearance? ever? at this point, or she still just &quot;Mentioned, but not seen&quot; Kind of like we only hear &quot;Blah blah blah&quot; Come out of the grown ups mouths...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, she is seen, but thankfully more as a presence than an actual fully speaking part (although she HAS dialogue). Rather than an active element, she is a plot device, or more accurately, a catalyst through which Charlie Brown's growth as a human being, his character development, is made possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh is the trick snoop does with his ears, a possible interprutation of the wayfare Art, or maybe a 5 dot specialty &quot;Wings Merit&quot; </div> </div> </div>EUREKA!<br /> <br /> Your post has just inspired me to figure out the PERFECT example of what a &quot;Bunk&quot; is!<br /> <br /> By all rights, Snoopy should NOT be able to fly his doghouse and fire an invisible machine gun to do battle with his Archnemesis, The Red Baron.<br /> <br /> And yet, through his &quot;Bunk&quot; of donning a red scarf, flight goggles, hopping on top of his Red Dog House while openly typing AND narrating &quot;It Was A Dark And Stormy Night&quot;, he opens a gateway into childhood wonder that takes him AND his Doghouse into the *Narrative Reality* of the raging heroic skies of World War I, perfectly working Pretend (Chimerical if you will) Machine Gun and all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> THAT is what a Bunk Is.<br /> <br /> A silly ritual that &quot;breaks the fourth wall&quot; and acknowledges the absurdity of dreams, thereby giving The Dreaming &quot;permission&quot; to flow through into the concious world. Snoopy is able to REALLY fly his Doghouse like a World War One Ace Flies his byplane because the through the NARRATIVE that his Bunk has written for his Cantrip, he has created a STAGE that allows this script/play to be real, and acted out as a (temporarily) living narrative that will end as soon as the curtains of reality close.<br /> <br /> A &quot;Bunk&quot;, in short, is the Pen/Typewriter in which you, the Director/Author of the Play/Story, can write and articulate the NARRATIVE that is the Cantrip on the Canvas/Paper of Banal-Reality so it is given on CREDIBLE context on which it can exist.<br /> <br /> Thank You For That, Prince of the Night! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 01-11-2016, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:32:45-08:00","id":806217,"title":"","content":"Oh! Another question on the two other shows? thought when you called bart a redcap... then what is Nelson, then thought... hes a thallain ogre.<br /> <br /> stupid, crude, rude and violent.<br /> <br /> Marge is likely a Boggan Grump, Kind honest, a trifle simple<br /> <br /> The flanders almost feel like Chimera<br /> <br /> in detective conan Professor Agasa is a Knocker Grump who just found his Niche<br /> <br /> he'd been inventing JUNK or thing that were &quot;Interesting&quot; perhaps but not genuinely useful until this VERY specific situation came along...<br /> <br /> Many knockers will probaly be this way to a degree.<br /> <br /> back on Peanuts<br /> <br /> oh is linuses blanket a treasure? Thought I should ask.<br /> <br /> Oh the Red Baron? is he likely a chimera? feels like he EXISTS just to be a nemesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"i